# LIVE (cloud) Supabase credentials — NAMES AND COMMENTS ONLY.
# Never put a real value here. Copy this file to `.env.cloud` and fill that in;
# `.env.cloud` is git-ignored. This template is committed via a `!` exception in
# .gitignore, the same arrangement as .env.example.
#
# Read by:
#   make pull-live     LIVE→local snapshot for testing against real data.
#                      Every live access is READ-ONLY; all writes are local.
#   make migrate-cloud / make seed-cloud   (via the environment)
#
# Why its own file rather than more keys in .env: `make setup-supabase`
# REWRITES .env with the LOCAL stack's values on every run, so cloud
# credentials kept there are both overwritten and one typo away from being
# used as if they were local.

# ── The cloud project's Postgres connection string ──────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Project Settings → Database → Connection string → URI.
#
# Prefer the DIRECT connection (db.<ref>.supabase.co:5432): pull-live runs
# pg_dump/pg_restore, which the TRANSACTION pooler (port 6543) cannot serve.
# Direct connections are IPv6-only unless the project has the IPv4 add-on, so
# on an IPv4-only network use the SESSION pooler (port 5432) instead — it
# speaks the full protocol and works with pg_dump.
#
# pull-live and migrate-cloud both REFUSE a localhost value, so this can never
# be pointed at the local stack by accident.
SUPABASE_DB_URL=

# ── The cloud project's service-role key ────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API. Server-only; it BYPASSES RLS, so it must
# never carry a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Used read-only by pull-live, to download
# live storage objects.
#
# Without it pull-live degrades to database-only: rows are restored but the
# image FILES are not, so every image 404s locally.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── The cloud project's API URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# e.g. https://<ref>.supabase.co
#
# pull-live restores rows VERBATIM, so any row holding an absolute cloud
# storage URL needs this host allowed by the dev CSP (next.config.ts widens it
# from this value). Omit it and the files sync correctly but the images are
# CSP-blocked — they render broken, which reads as a data bug rather than a
# missing config line.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
